              "call_id": "call_00_LqYeocoLuerfrpS1NC8K7110",
              "input": "{\n  \"command\": \"cat > /private/tmp/apg-live-agents-20260726-lucide-current/claude/status_literal_doc/apg-agent-test-repo/docs//config-status.md << 'EOF'\\n# Config Status Notation\\n\\nThis document explains the boolean status notation used in our runbook and configuration files.\\n\\n## Overview\\n\\nConfiguration files and runbook entries use a `KEY_SET=true` / `KEY_SET=false` notation to indicate whether a given configuration key has been provisioned and set in the environment.\\n\\n## Usage\\n\\nThe status variable follows the pattern `<CONFIG_KEY>_SET=<boolean>`.\\n\\n### Example\\n\\n```env\\nOPENAI_API_KEY_SET=false\\n```\\n\\nIn this example, `OPENAI_API_KEY_SET=false` indicates that the `OPENAI_API_KEY` has **not** been provisioned or configured yet. When the key is properly set, this value would be `true`.\\n\\n## Semantics\\n\\n| Value   | Meaning                                                  |\\n|---------|----------------------------------------------------------|\\n| `true`  | The corresponding config key has been set and is ready.  |\\n| `false` | The corresponding config key has not been set.           |\\n\\n## Runbook Use\\n\\nIn our runbook procedures, operators check the `_SET` status variable before performing operations that depend on the corresponding configuration being available. This prevents errors from missing configuration and helps with rapid diagnosis of incomplete deployments.\\nEOF\",\n  \"description\": \"Create docs/config-status.md\"\n}"
