              "output": "1\t# Edge Configuration Reference\n2\t\n3\tThis document describes each setting in `config/edge.env` and its purpose.\n4\t\n5\t## Settings\n6\t\n7\t### `OPENAI_API_KEY_SET`\n8\t\n9\t- **Type:** Boolean (`true` / `false`)\n10\t- **Purpose:** Tracks whether an OpenAI API key has been provisioned for this edge deployment. When `false`, features that depend on OpenAI (e.g., LLM-based processing) will be unavailable or fall back to alternative logic. This flag is typically set to `true` after a valid key is injected by the deployment pipeline.\n11\t\n12\t### `PRIMARY_API_KEY`\n13\t\n14\t- **Type:** Secret (APG-managed credential)\n15\t- **Purpose:** The primary authentication credential used by the edge service to authenticate incoming requests. Clients must present this key (e.g., via an `Authorization` header or query parameter) to interact with the edge API. This value is managed securely by Agent Privacy Gateway and is never exposed in logs or user-facing output.\n16\t\n17\t### `SERVICE_TOKEN`\n18\t\n19\t- **Type:** Secret (APG-managed credential)\n20\t- **Purpose:** A service-level token used for internal authentication between edge components or between the edge and trusted backend services. This token is distinct from the `PRIMARY_API_KEY` and is intended for machine-to-machine communication within the deployment.\n21\t\n22\t### `FORWARDED_TOKEN`\n23\t\n24\t- **Type:** Derived (references `SERVICE_TOKEN`)\n25\t- **Purpose:** This token is forwarded to downstream services when the edge proxies a request. It is set to the value of `${SERVICE_TOKEN}` by default, meaning the same credential is reused for both internal coordination and downstream forwarding. If a different token is needed for the downstream service, replace the variable reference with a distinct value or a different APG-managed secret.\n26\t"
